
TABS(1)             UNIX Programmer's Manual              TABS(1)

NAME
     tabs - set terminal tabs

SYNOPSIS
     tabs [ -n ] [ terminal ]

DESCRIPTION
     _T_a_b_s sets the tabs on a variety of terminals.  Various of
     the terminal names given in _t_e_r_m(7) are recognized; the
     default is, however, suitable for most 300 baud terminals.
     If the -n flag is present then the left margin is not
     indented as is normal.

SEE ALSO
     stty(1), tset(1), tabs(7)

